doc ///
    Key
        k3Families
    Headline
        list the supported K3 surface families
    Usage
        k3Families()
    Description
        Example
            k3Families()
            original = k3Surface 2;
            original#"recipe"#"family"
            spec = hashTable {"family" => "quartic_with_line"};
            marked = realizeK3Surface k3Recipe spec;
            marked#"lattice"#"gram"
        Text
            The marked quartic families are @TT "quartic_with_line"@ and @TT "quartic_with_conic"@.
            The degree parameter @TT "d"@ defaults to 2 for these families. The seed and prime
            characteristic have the same defaults as for @TO k3Surface@. The @TT "K3Surfaces"@
            package constructs a quartic and its smooth rational curve. The model also marks
            a rational point on the curve for the point sheaves in the original study.
    SeeAlso
        k3Recipe
        markedCurveClass
        markedQuarticSpec
///

doc ///
    Key
        markedCurveClass
        (markedCurveClass, K3Surface)
        markedCurveSheaf
        (markedCurveSheaf, K3Surface)
    Headline
        the divisor class and structure sheaf of a marked curve
    Usage
        C = markedCurveClass K
        F = markedCurveSheaf K
    Inputs
        K:K3Surface
            a quartic with a marked line or conic
    Outputs
        C:DivisorClass
        F:CoherentSheaf
    Description
        Text
            The marked basis is $(H,C)$. The intersection numbers are $H^2=4$,
            $H\cdot C=\deg C$ and $C^2=-2$ by adjunction on the smooth quartic.
            These give the sublattice generated by the polarization and the marked curve.
            The ideal of the curve is available under @TT "curve"@ in @TT "markedIdeals"@.
            The structure sheaf is viewed as a sheaf on the quartic.
        Example
            K = realizeK3Surface k3Recipe hashTable {"family" => "quartic_with_conic"};
            C = markedCurveClass K;
            divisorPairing(K#"polarization", C)
            cohomologyDims markedCurveSheaf K
///

doc ///
    Key
        markedQuarticSpec
        (markedQuarticSpec, K3Surface)
    Headline
        save the data needed to reconstruct an exact marked quartic
    Usage
        spec = markedQuarticSpec K
    Inputs
        K:K3Surface
            a quartic with a marked line or conic
    Outputs
        spec:HashTable
            a recipe with explicit equation and markings
    Description
        Text
            The @TT "model"@ table contains one quartic polynomial under @TT "equation"@,
            two curve generators under @TT "curve"@, and three linear point generators
            under @TT "point"@. Each polynomial is a list of terms of the form
            @TT "{{e0, e1, e2, e3}, coefficient}"@ in the ordered ambient coordinates.
            Coefficients are integers modulo the characteristic. Reload the data using
            @TO k3Recipe@ and @TO realizeK3Surface@. The actual marked ideals travel
            with the surface in batch tasks that use an explicit model.
        Example
            K = realizeK3Surface k3Recipe hashTable {"family" => "quartic_with_line"};
            spec = markedQuarticSpec K;
            T = realizeK3Surface k3Recipe spec;
            markedQuarticSpec T === spec
            cohomologyDims markedCurveSheaf T
///
